Third-party designs
===================

solarian_arm1/assets/
  The solarian-arm1 mechanical design, its meshes and its MuJoCo model are
  derived from the SO-ARM100 (Standard Open Arm 100) by The Robot Studio
  (https://github.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100), Apache License 2.0, and
  modified, including an added wrist yaw joint and different servos.
  Meshes named so_arm100_* and sts3215_* come from that design.

STL/, STEP/, docs/media/ and tools/assembly_render/cad/
  Print-ready wrist parts, CAD export and renders of solarian-arm1. The
  stock arm parts in them (meshes named Base_08q, Rotation_Pitch_08i,
  SO_ARM100_08k_* and STS3215_03a*) come from the SO-ARM100 design above.
  STS3215_Side_bracket and STS3215_End_bracket are imported models of the
  standard sheet-metal STS3215 servo brackets. The renders in docs/media also
  show solarian-gripper1 (https://github.com/solarian-dev/solarian-gripper1);
  see that repository's NOTICE for its third-party designs.

